---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="A cache and a database disagree" hint="Replay two situations from Meta's 2022 post in a simplified form: a slow fill racing a newer write, and an error handler that fails to drop a stale entry. Change the cache's rules and see what it holds at the end. A teaching model with made-up version numbers, not Meta's code.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Press <b>Reset</b>. With <b>Scenario</b> on the fill race, <b>Version handling</b> on <b>None</b> and the fill reply <b>late</b>, the old reply overwrites the newer value: the cache ends with <b>x=42 at version 1</b> while the database holds <b>x=43 at version 2</b>, and a checker would still see it as wrong.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Version handling</b> to <b>Version stored in the entry</b>: the cache ignores the older reply and ends with <b>x=43 at version 2</b>, which matches.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Entry evicted before the late reply</b> to <b>Yes</b>: with no entry left, the cache has no version to compare with, takes the old reply, and ends with <b>x=42 at version 1</b> again.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Version handling</b> to <b>Version kept after eviction</b> (my own teaching idea, not something the post says Meta does): the cache still knows version 2 existed, ignores the old reply, and ends with <b>no entry</b>, so the next read fills it from the database and matches.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Scenario</b> to the error handler: with a transient error and the handler that drops <b>only if the version is lower</b>, the stale entry <b>metadata=0 at version 4</b> stays. Set the handler to drop <b>whatever the version</b> and the entry is dropped, so the next read matches.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg bki" data-bki>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Scenario <select class="pg-in" data-sc><option value="race">A slow fill races a newer write</option><option value="error">An error in the invalidation handler</option></select></label>
      <label>Version handling <select class="pg-in" data-ver><option value="none">None, last arrival wins</option><option value="version">Version stored in the entry</option><option value="remember">Version kept after eviction</option></select></label>
      <label>Fill reply arrives <select class="pg-in" data-ord><option value="late">After the invalidation</option><option value="early">Before the invalidation</option></select></label>
      <label>Entry evicted before the late reply <select class="pg-in" data-ev><option value="no">No</option><option value="yes">Yes</option></select></label>
      <label>Transient error during invalidation <select class="pg-in" data-er><option value="yes">Yes</option><option value="no">No</option></select></label>
      <label>Error handler drops the entry <select class="pg-in" data-hd><option value="lower">Only if its version is lower</option><option value="always">Whatever its version</option></select></label>
      <button type="button" class="btn" data-reset>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Database holds</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Cache holds at the end</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Cache and database agree</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>A Polaris-style check</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="bki-wrap">
      <p class="pg-note bki-cap">What happens, in order:</p>
      <ol class="bki-log" data-log></ol>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Teaching model with made-up version numbers, not Meta's code or data. Race: the cache starts a fill that reads x=42 at version 1; a write then sets x=43 at version 2 in the database, and its invalidation tells the cache x=43 at version 2. The slow fill reply arrives either before or after that invalidation. With no version handling the last arrival wins. With version handling an arriving value is ignored if its version is not newer than the entry's. An eviction removes the entry, and only the third option remembers the evicted version. Error: the cache holds metadata=0 at version 4, the database holds metadata=1 at version 4, and the invalidation normally replaces the entry. On a transient error the handler runs instead. In this model a stale entry stays until something changes it, and a missing entry is refilled from the database on the next read. The check mimics what Meta's 2022 post describes for Polaris: it looks again after a timescale of one and five minutes before calling an entry inconsistent. The option that keeps versions after eviction is my own idea for teaching, and the post does not say how Meta fixed either problem.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<style>
  .bki-wrap { display: grid; gap: 6px; }
  .bki-cap { margin: 0; }
  .bki-log { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.4rem; display: grid; gap: 4px; font-size: .92rem; }
  .bki-log li { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
<script>
  import { query } from '../../playground';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-bki]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const select = (k: string) => q<HTMLSelectElement>(`[data-${k}]`);
    const DEFAULTS: Record<string, string> = { sc: 'race', ver: 'none', ord: 'late', ev: 'no', er: 'yes', hd: 'lower' };
    type Entry = { value: number; version: number } | null;
    const show = (e: Entry) => (e ? (e.version === 4 ? `metadata=${e.value} at version 4` : `x=${e.value} at version ${e.version}`) : 'no entry');

    function draw() {
      const sc = select('sc').value, ver = select('ver').value, ord = select('ord').value;
      const ev = select('ev').value === 'yes', err = select('er').value === 'yes', hd = select('hd').value;
      const race = sc === 'race';
      ['ver', 'ord'].forEach((k) => (select(k).disabled = !race));
      select('ev').disabled = !race || ord === 'early';
      select('er').disabled = race;
      select('hd').disabled = race || !err;
      const log: string[] = [];
      let entry: Entry; let db: Entry; let remembered = 0;
      const accept = (value: number, version: number, what: string) => {
        const newest = Math.max(entry ? entry.version : 0, ver === 'remember' ? remembered : 0);
        if (ver !== 'none' && newest >= version) log.push(`${what}: version ${version} is not newer than version ${newest}, so the cache ignores it`);
        else { entry = { value, version }; log.push(`${what}: the cache stores x=${value} at version ${version}`); }
      };
      if (race) {
        entry = null; db = { value: 43, version: 2 };
        log.push('The cache starts a fill and the database answers x=42 at version 1, but the reply is slow');
        log.push('A write sets x=43 at version 2 in the database, and an invalidation is sent');
        if (ord === 'early') { accept(42, 1, 'The fill reply arrives'); accept(43, 2, 'The invalidation arrives'); }
        else {
          accept(43, 2, 'The invalidation arrives');
          if (ev) { if (ver === 'remember' && entry) remembered = (entry as { version: number }).version; entry = null; log.push('The entry is evicted to make room'); }
          accept(42, 1, 'The late fill reply arrives');
        }
      } else {
        entry = { value: 0, version: 4 }; db = { value: 1, version: 4 };
        log.push('The cache holds metadata=0 at version 4 after a fill that overlapped a database transaction');
        if (!err) { entry = { value: 1, version: 4 }; log.push('The invalidation arrives and the cache stores metadata=1 at version 4'); }
        else if (hd === 'lower') log.push('The invalidation hits a transient error. The handler drops the entry only if its version is lower than 4, but it is 4, so nothing is dropped');
        else { entry = null; log.push('The invalidation hits a transient error. The handler drops the entry whatever its version'); }
      }
      const e = entry as Entry; const d = db as { value: number; version: number };
      const agree = e === null || (e.value === d.value && e.version === d.version);
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = show(d);
      q('[data-n1]').textContent = 'the source of truth';
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = show(e);
      q('[data-n2]').textContent = e ? 'stays until something changes it' : 'the next read fills it from the database';
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = agree ? 'yes' : 'no';
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = agree ? (e ? 'the same value and version' : 'nothing stale is left in the cache') : 'the cache serves a stale value';
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = agree ? 'passes' : 'reports it';
      q('[data-n4]').textContent = agree ? 'no mismatch at second 0, or none left after retries' : 'still wrong after 1 minute and after 5 minutes';
      ['b1', 'b2', 'b3', 'b4'].forEach((b, i) => q<HTMLElement>(`[data-${b}]`).style.setProperty('--c', i > 0 && !agree ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)'));
      const list = q('[data-log]'); list.replaceChildren(...log.map((t) => { const li = document.createElement('li'); li.textContent = t; return li; }));
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); out.classList.toggle('bad', !agree);
      out.textContent = agree ? `Consistent: the cache ends with ${show(e)}${e ? '' : ', and a read refills it'}, matching ${show(d)}.` : `Inconsistent: the cache holds ${show(e)} but the database holds ${show(d)}, and nothing in this model repairs it.`;
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw);
    root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    q('[data-reset]').addEventListener('click', () => { Object.keys(DEFAULTS).forEach((k) => (select(k).value = DEFAULTS[k])); draw(); });
    draw();
  });
</script>
